# Rosigma vehicles that drive during the battle. A soldier on a driver seat switches on
# drive mode with the Drive button or the drive hotkey (D), then clicks where to go: the
# first click previews the route, the second drives. Turrets can't drive (they can't walk).
# Rosigma terrain is tough: most of its walls have 50 to 100 armor. Each vehicle has its own
# time units per turn, so swapping drivers doesn't make it go further. Driven onto an
# enemy, a vehicle hits it with its run over damage; whoever survives stops it (rammed).
crafts:
  # Three Chimeras on one craft map, each a vehicle of its own. Each driver seat is the
  # front-left tile of its troop bay (the front is the south end of the map). Up to 12 tiles a turn.
  - type: STR_CHIMERA
    battleVehicle:
      driverSeats: [[1, 6, 0], [7, 10, 0], [2, 17, 0]]
      tuPerTile: 4
      timeUnits: 48
      crushArmor: 100
      runOverDamage: 150
  - type: STR_CHIMERASL
    battleVehicle:
      driverSeats: [[1, 6, 0], [7, 10, 0], [2, 17, 0]]
      tuPerTile: 4
      timeUnits: 48
      crushArmor: 100
      runOverDamage: 150
  # The Baneblade is one big vehicle (the trailer at the back is part of it). Its driver
  # seats are the small command post beside the turret basket, on level 1. Slow and heavy:
  # up to 8 tiles a turn, through almost anything.
  - type: STR_BANEBLADE
    battleVehicle:
      driverSeats: [[5, 8, 1], [4, 8, 1]]
      tuPerTile: 6
      timeUnits: 48
      crushArmor: 254
      runOverDamage: 300
